  "aboutCreditsTitle": "Credits and licences",
  "aboutCreditsBody": "Country borders: Natural Earth, public domain. Flags: the flag-icons set, MIT licence. Fonts: Manrope (SIL Open Font License) and Roboto (Apache 2.0). Built with Flutter (BSD).",
  "aboutCopyright": "© 2026 Domiday. All rights reserved.",
  "aboutNoWarranty": "The app is provided as is, without warranty. It does not determine residency, entry eligibility or visa limits.",
  "aboutTitle": "About Domiday",
  "aboutVersion": "Personal journal · {version}",
  "@aboutVersion": {"placeholders": {"version": {"type": "String"}}},
  "aboutPlaceTitle": "Current place and history",
  "aboutPlaceBody": "A manual journal of trips and of where you are now. It answers “when and where were we” and never changes anything by itself: every record, date and country is entered or confirmed by you.",
  "aboutUnknownTitle": "Unknown does not mean home",
  "aboutUnknownBody": "The home country is your personal setting, not tax residency. Changing it recalculates the categories but does not change the records. Without an arrival date the current stay adds no days to the totals. Unknown days are counted from 1 January to today, and for past years — for the whole year. Gaps between known stays can be recorded as days at home only after reviewing the dates and your confirmation. Those records can be edited or deleted in the journal.",
  "aboutDeviceTitle": "Your records stay on your device",
  "aboutDeviceBody": "Data is stored in the app’s private folder. There is no account, cloud, network requests, ads or analytics. A backup — a file in the app’s format — can be saved and restored from Settings. Uninstalling the app or clearing its data will lose the records. Do not keep the only copy of important information here.",
  "aboutCountingTitle": "How days are counted",
  "aboutCountingBody": "The arrival and departure days are included: a one-day trip is one day. Overlapping records do not increase the total. Within one country overlapping days also count once. A moving day may belong to two countries, so the sum by country may exceed the total number of days. With a year selected, only days in that year are counted; cards keep the full trip dates. Searching by year finds trips that touch it but does not trim dates by itself.",
  "aboutNotVisaTitle": "Not a visa or tax calculator",
  "aboutNotVisaBody": "The totals describe only the entered records, not your whole history of stays. A missed trip is unknown history, not proof of absence from a country. The journal does not determine residency, the right to enter or compliance with visa limits.",

